    "report_label": "unshadowed DIRSPLITS=2 DIRECTIONAL",
    "compile_only_label": "sibling-family over-reach checks",
    "count_exemption_axis": null,
    "note": "Consumer-local admission gate. Each entry pins three things measured from a native archive blob - its declaration set, the set of constant-buffer registers its body reads, and how many times it reads each - and the check passes only when the reconstruction compiled from that blob's own macro set agrees. The pinned values come from the game bytecode, never from this repo's output. This is an ABI and constant-read claim only, not an execution-equivalence claim; execution proof stays with the producer oracle in the sibling fallout4-re. No entry is exempt from the read-count check, so the manifest declares no count_exemption_axis. dcl_temps is excluded because it is register allocation, not ABI.",
    "evidence": "Declarations, read-sets and read-counts were measured by disassembling each of the five blobs with fxc /dumpbin, each read against its own constant table. No register role or body logic was transferred from the no-SHADOW SPOT blobs. Absent SHADOW, the declaration set collapses to four g-buffer texture2d reads and four mode_default samplers with no shadow resource at all, so the three declaration groups here differ only in constant-buffer size, and the size is a function of the reads: SPECULAR adds the cb12[30] gloss term and raises CB12 to 31, and AMBIENT adds the cb2[6..8] gradient rows and raises CB2 to 9. Those three rows are one DirectionalAmbient constant of register_count 3, not a split/fade pair. DIRSPLITS=2 is the decoder baseline for these entries and no two-cascade behaviour is claimed: the CB2 read-set is exactly {0,1,2} or {0,1,2,6,7,8}, and SplitDistances, FadeDistances and every Shadow* constant are absent from all five constant tables, so no split-distance, cascade-projection or shadow filter register is allocated, let alone read. IGNOREROUGHNESS is reconstructed, not exempted - it removes the roughness-driven visibility geometry and the rim term, which accounts exactly for the two cb2[1] reads and one cb2[2] read it drops, while leaving the material-code-1 hair specular path untouched (cb12[28] holds at 4 reads, cb12[29] at 2, and both sincos lobes survive) and leaving the cb2[6..8] ambient gradient untouched."
  },
